<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly lower.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly lower.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) fell across most maturities on Thursday, while the one-year rate was steady, traders said.</p>
<p>The general decline in PHIBOR rates followed the easing of rates at the money market, they said.</p>
<p>The one-year rate, however, was unchanged since it was less vulnerable to changes in the overnight rates, dealers said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  SEPT 26		 SEPT 25</p>
<p>    1 W		12  7/16		12 11/16</p>
<p>    2 W		12  5/16		12  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		12  3/16		12  5/16</p>
<p>    2 M		12			12</p>
<p>    3 M		11  7/8		 11 15/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11 15/16		12</p>
<p>    12M		12  1/8		 12  1/8</p>
<p>    VAL		27-Sep		  26-Sep</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
